ce:section.ce:para:
Results on biogas formation after punctual loadings (Fig. 4
                        ) suggest that the amount and rate of biogas production depend on the quantity of added organic material and can be well controlled and predicted. The amount of the produced biogas increased with higher punctual loading while the velocity of degradation of the added organic material decreased with higher punctual loading (Fig. 4). The thermophilic process temperature was advantageous over mesophilic digestion conditions as, with exception of the punctual loading of 4gVS
                        L−1, a more rapid and higher methane production was observed. Furthermore, the decrease in methane content of the biogas produced after punctual loading and the effects on pH-value within the reactor was less pronounced under thermophilic temperature conditions (Tables 3 and 4).
